.TH BIOSEQ.FASTA 4 2000-1月 "slicer" "slicer"
.SH NAME
slicer \- create a sequence region slicer for cut a specific sequence region from
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIslicer(\fBfa\fR as any, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
create a sequence region slicer for cut a specific sequence region from 
 the given sequence data
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfa\fB \fR\- 
 the target sequence data source, which can be:
 
 1. a @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.FASTA.FastaSeq\fR sequence object, then a 
    @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.Slicer.FastaSlicer\fR will be created;
 2. a chromosome or contigs sequence object(@\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.NucleotideModels.ChunkedNtFasta\fR) 
    that is read from the genome assembly sequence file via the 
    \fBread_assembly\fR api, then a @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.Slicer.ChunkSlicer\fR will be created;
 3. a ncbi genbank database file object(\fBGBFF.File\fR), then a 
    @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.Slicer.GenBankSlicer\fR will be created.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment object.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
an @\fBT:SMRUCC.genomics.SequenceModel.Slicer.ISlicer\fR object for slice the sequence region from the 
 given sequence data source;
 
 this function returns a R# error message object if the given sequence data 
 source is not a supported sequence data model.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
the slicer object is used for cut a sequence region from a huge genome 
 sequence in a memory efficient manner, which is very helpful for the 
 sequence data extraction of a specific gene locus site.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
bioseq.fasta
.SH FILES
.PP
seqtoolkit.dll
.PP
